/-!
# Slicing a flat algebra by an element that is a nonzerodivisor on a fibre

Let `A → B` be a ring map, let `q ⊆ B` be a prime lying over `p ⊆ A`, and let `h ∈ q`. Assume
`A → B` is flat and that the image of `h` in the fibre `B_q / p B_q` is a nonzerodivisor. The
Stacks Project's proof of Tag 056Y (slicing a flat morphism of finite presentation by a local
equation) reduces, after a Noetherian approximation, to the following purely algebraic claim:

> after replacing `B` by a localization `B_g` with `g ∉ q`, the element `h` becomes a
> nonzerodivisor and `B/hB` becomes flat over `A`.

This file proves that claim for Noetherian `A` and `B` with `A → B` of finite type. The two
halves are proved separately and have different engines:

* that `h` becomes a nonzerodivisor after localizing away from one element comes from the
  annihilator of `h` being finitely generated, i.e. from Stacks Tag 061L;
* that `B/hB` becomes flat comes from openness of the flat locus, Stacks Tag 00RC, together
  with the local statement Stacks Tag 00MF.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Flatness.mem_nonZeroDivisors_atPrime_and_flat_quotient_of_fibre`: Stacks Tag 00MF
  applied at `q`, with the fibre written as a quotient of `B_q` by the ideal generated by `p`
  rather than by the maximal ideal of `A_p`. This is the local half of the claim: `h` is already
  a nonzerodivisor in `B_q`, and `B_q / h B_q` is already flat over `A`.
* `Stacks.Flatness.exists_notMem_mem_nonZeroDivisors_away`: the nonzerodivisor half of the
  claim.
* `Stacks.Flatness.exists_notMem_forall_flat_localizedModule_quotient`: the flatness half of the
  claim, in the pointwise form that openness of the flat locus delivers.
* `Stacks.Flatness.exists_notMem_mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_and_forall_flat`: the two halves
  together, which is the algebraic claim of Tag 056Y.

Two reusable bricks come out on the way:

* `Stacks.Flatness.localizedModuleQuotientSpanEquiv`: localizing the ring quotient `B / hB` at a
  submonoid `p` of `B` gives the quotient of `Localization p` by the ideal generated by the image
  of `h`. This is the identification that lets the conclusion of Tag 00MF (a quotient of a
  localization) be fed to Tag 00RC (a localization of a quotient).
* `Stacks.Flatness.flat_localizedModule_quotient_iff`: the same identification read as an
  equivalence of flatness statements over the base.

## Implementation notes

**Why the flatness conclusion is pointwise.** Openness of the flat locus (Tag 00RC) is a
statement about the set of primes `q'` of `B` at which `(B/hB)_{q'}` is flat over `A`, so what it
delivers is a basic open `D(g)` inside that locus, i.e. flatness of `(B/hB)_{q'}` for every prime
`q'` with `g ∉ q'`. Passing from there to `Module.Flat A (B_g / h B_g)` is a local-global
principle for flatness over a basic open, and it is **not** available: Mathlib's
`Module.flat_of_isLocalized_maximal` is stated for the maximal ideals of the ring over which the
module lives, so applying it at `B_g` requires identifying `((B/hB)_g)_P` with `(B/hB)_{q'}` for
`q'` the contraction of `P`, i.e. a transitivity statement for `IsLocalizedModule` at nested
submonoids. `Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LocalizedModule.Basic`'s `IsLocalizedModule.liftOfLE` is the
nested-submonoid comparison, but it is stated for submonoids of the *base* ring, not for the
`P.primeCompl` that `flat_of_isLocalized_maximal` demands. That single missing step is all that
separates the pointwise conclusion here from the ring-level one.

**Universes.** Everything is stated at arbitrary, independent universes for `A` and `B`; nothing
in the argument constrains them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 056Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/056Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00MF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00RC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00RC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 061L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/061L)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing RingTheory.Sequence

namespace Stacks.Flatness

section Bridge

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] (pm : Submonoid B) (h : B)

/-- Localizing the ring quotient `B / hB` at a submonoid `pm` of `B` gives the quotient of
`Localization pm` by the ideal generated by the image of `h`.

This is the identification that lets a conclusion about `Localization pm ⧸ (h)` — the shape that
Stacks Tag 00MF produces — be read as a conclusion about `LocalizedModule pm (B ⧸ (h))`, the
shape that Stacks Tag 00RC consumes. It is an `A`-linear equivalence because every map in sight
is `B`-linear. -/
noncomputable def localizedModuleQuotientSpanEquiv :
    (Localization pm ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap B (Localization pm) h}) ≃ₗ[A]
      LocalizedModule pm (B ⧸ Ideal.span {h}) :=
  let N : Submodule B B := Ideal.span {h}
  have hspan : N.localized' (Localization pm) pm (Algebra.linearMap B (Localization pm)) =
      Ideal.span {algebraMap B (Localization pm) h} := by
    rw [show N = Ideal.span {h} from rfl, Submodule.localized'_span]
    simp
  ((Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ hspan.symm).restrictScalars A).trans
    ((IsLocalizedModule.linearEquiv pm
      (N.toLocalizedQuotient' (Localization pm) pm (Algebra.linearMap B (Localization pm)))
      (LocalizedModule.mkLinearMap pm (B ⧸ N))).restrictScalars A)

/-- Flatness over the base of the quotient of `Localization pm` by the image of `h` is the same
as flatness of the localization at `pm` of the ring quotient `B / hB`. -/
theorem flat_localizedModule_quotient_iff :
    Module.Flat A (Localization pm ⧸ Ideal.span {algebraMap B (Localization pm) h}) ↔
      Module.Flat A (LocalizedModule pm (B ⧸ Ideal.span {h})) :=
  ⟨fun _ => Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (localizedModuleQuotientSpanEquiv pm h).symm,
    fun _ => Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (localizedModuleQuotientSpanEquiv pm h)⟩

end Bridge

section Local

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsNoetherianRing B] [Module.Flat A B]

open Module.Flat

/-- **Stacks Tag 00MF at a prime of a flat algebra.** Let `A → B` be flat with `A` and `B`
Noetherian, let `q` be a prime of `B` and `p = q ∩ A` its contraction. If the image of `h` in the
fibre `B_q / p B_q` is a nonzerodivisor, then `h` is already a nonzerodivisor in `B_q` and
`B_q / h B_q` is already flat over `A`.

This is the local half of the algebraic claim in the proof of Stacks Tag 056Y. The fibre is
written as the quotient of `B_q` by the ideal generated by the image of `p`, which is where the
geometric statement presents it; Tag 00MF itself is stated with the maximal ideal of `A_p`, and
the two ideals agree. -/
@[sga "3 V 7.2" "more general"]
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_atPrime_and_flat_quotient_of_fibre (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] {h : B}
    (hreg : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (q.comap (algebraMap A B))) (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
        Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)) (q.comap (algebraMap A B)))) :
    algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q) ∧
      Module.Flat A (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
        Ideal.span {algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h}) := by
  set p : Ideal A := q.comap (algebraMap A B)
  have : p.IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  have : q.LiesOver p := ⟨rfl⟩
  let _ := Localization.AtPrime.algebraOfLiesOver p q
  have hmap : Ideal.map (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime q))
      (maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p)) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)) p := by
    rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal, Ideal.map_map,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime q)]
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime q)) := by
    rw [Localization.AtPrime.algebraMap_eq]
    infer_instance
  have key :=
    mem_nonZeroDivisors_and_flat_quotient_span_singleton_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors_maximalIdeal
      (R := Localization.AtPrime p) (S := Localization.AtPrime q)
      (f := algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h) (by rwa [hmap])
  exact ⟨key.1, (Module.flat_iff_of_isLocalization (R := A) (Localization.AtPrime p)
    p.primeCompl _).mp key.2⟩

end Local

section Away

variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B]

/-- Being a nonzerodivisor in a localization away from `g` is an elementwise condition on the
annihilator: `h` is a nonzerodivisor in `B_g` exactly when every element of `B` killed by `h` is
killed by a power of `g`.

This form is *monotone* in `g` — replacing `g` by a multiple of it preserves it, which the
`nonZeroDivisors` form does not visibly do — and that is what lets two separately chosen
localizations be combined. -/
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_iff (g h : B) :
    algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.Away g) ↔
      ∀ b : B, h * b = 0 → ∃ n : ℕ, g ^ n * b = 0 := by
  have hzero : ∀ b : B, algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) b = 0 ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, g ^ n * b = 0 := by
    intro b
    rw [IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers g)]
    exact ⟨fun ⟨⟨s, n, hn⟩, hs⟩ => ⟨n, by simpa [hn, mul_comm] using hs⟩,
      fun ⟨n, hn⟩ => ⟨⟨g ^ n, n, rfl⟩, by simpa [mul_comm] using hn⟩⟩
  rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff]
  refine ⟨fun hreg b hb => (hzero b).mp (hreg.1 _ (by rw [← map_mul, hb, map_zero])),
    fun hmon => ?_⟩
  have key : ∀ x : Localization.Away g,
      algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h * x = 0 → x = 0 := by
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨n, a, ha⟩ := IsLocalization.Away.surj g z
    have hA : algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) (h * a) = 0 := by
      rw [map_mul, ← ha, ← mul_assoc, hz, zero_mul]
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := (hzero _).mp hA
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hmon (g ^ m * a) (by rw [← mul_assoc, mul_comm h, mul_assoc, hm])
    have haz : algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) a = 0 :=
      (hzero a).mpr ⟨k + m, by rwa [pow_add, mul_assoc]⟩
    exact (IsUnit.mul_left_eq_zero
      (IsLocalization.Away.algebraMap_pow_isUnit g n)).mp (ha.trans haz)
  exact ⟨key, fun x hx => key x (by rwa [mul_comm])⟩

/-- A nonzerodivisor in `B_g` stays a nonzerodivisor in `B_{g g'}`. -/
theorem mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_mul_right {g h : B}
    (hreg : algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.Away g))
    (g' : B) :
    algebraMap B (Localization.Away (g * g')) h ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization.Away (g * g')) := by
  rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_iff] at hreg ⊢
  intro b hb
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hreg b hb
  exact ⟨n, by rw [mul_pow, mul_comm (g ^ n), mul_assoc, hn, mul_zero]⟩

end Away

section Spread

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- **The nonzerodivisor half of the algebraic claim of Stacks Tag 056Y.** If `h` lies in a prime
`q` of a Noetherian ring `B` and becomes a nonzerodivisor in `B_q`, then it becomes a
nonzerodivisor already in `B_g` for some `g ∉ q`.

The hypothesis `h ∈ q` is what makes the one-term sequence `[h]` *regular* rather than merely
weakly regular over `B_q`, which is what the spreading-out statement Stacks Tag 061L consumes;
mathematically it says that the annihilator of `h`, being finitely generated, is killed by a
single element outside `q`. -/
theorem exists_notMem_mem_nonZeroDivisors_away [IsNoetherianRing B] (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime]
    {h : B} (hhq : h ∈ q)
    (hreg : algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    ∃ g ∈ q.primeCompl,
      algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.Away g) := by
  have hmax : algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h ∈
      maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
    rw [← Localization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hhq
  have hweak : IsWeaklyRegular (LocalizedModule q.primeCompl B)
      [algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h] := by
    rw [isWeaklyRegular_cons_iff]
    exact ⟨(isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.mpr hreg).left, IsWeaklyRegular.nil _ _⟩
  have hpreg : IsRegular (LocalizedModule q.primeCompl B)
      [algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h] :=
    IsRegular.of_isWeaklyRegular_of_mem_maximalIdeal _
      (by simpa using hmax) hweak
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hgreg⟩ := regular_sequence_localize_away_of_atPrime q [h] (by simpa using hpreg)
  refine ⟨g, hg, ?_⟩
  have hw := hgreg.toIsWeaklyRegular
  rw [show List.map (⇑(algebraMap B (Localization.Away g))) [h] =
    [algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h] from rfl, isWeaklyRegular_cons_iff] at hw
  rw [← isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors]
  exact isLeftRegular_iff_isRegular.mp hw.1

/-- **The flatness half of the algebraic claim of Stacks Tag 056Y.** Let `A` be Noetherian, `B` a
finite type `A`-algebra, and `q` a prime of `B` at which `B/hB` is flat over `A`. Then `B/hB` is
flat over `A` at every prime of a basic open neighbourhood of `q`.

This is openness of the flat locus, Stacks Tag 00RC over a Noetherian base, together with the
fact that the basic opens are a basis of the Zariski topology. -/
theorem exists_notMem_forall_flat_localizedModule_quotient [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Algebra.FiniteType A B] (q : Ideal B) [hq : q.IsPrime] {h : B}
    (hflatq : Module.Flat A (LocalizedModule.AtPrime q (B ⧸ Ideal.span {h}))) :
    ∃ g ∈ q.primeCompl, ∀ q' : Ideal B, ∀ _ : q'.IsPrime, g ∉ q' →
      Module.Flat A (LocalizedModule.AtPrime q' (B ⧸ Ideal.span {h})) := by
  have hopen := Module.isOpen_setOf_flat_localizedModule_atPrime_of_isNoetherianRing
    (R := A) (S := B) (M := B ⧸ Ideal.span {h})
  obtain ⟨V, ⟨g, rfl⟩, hmem, hsub⟩ :=
    PrimeSpectrum.isTopologicalBasis_basic_opens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (a := (⟨q, hq⟩ : PrimeSpectrum B)) hflatq hopen
  exact ⟨g, hmem, fun q' hq' hgq' =>
    hsub (show (⟨q', hq'⟩ : PrimeSpectrum B) ∈ PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen g from hgq')⟩

/-- **The algebraic claim in the proof of Stacks Tag 056Y.** Let `A → B` be a flat ring map of
finite type between Noetherian rings, let `q` be a prime of `B` and `p = q ∩ A`. Let `h ∈ q` map
to a nonzerodivisor in the fibre `B_q / p B_q`. Then there is `g ∉ q` such that

* `h` is a nonzerodivisor in `B_g`, and
* `B/hB` is flat over `A` at every prime of `B` not containing `g`.

The second conclusion is the pointwise form of "`B_g / h B_g` is flat over `A`"; see the
implementation notes of this file for the one local-global step that separates them. -/
theorem exists_notMem_mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_and_forall_flat [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [Module.Flat A B]
    (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime] {h : B} (hhq : h ∈ q)
    (hreg : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q))
        (q.comap (algebraMap A B))) (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime q) h) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q ⧸
        Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.AtPrime q)) (q.comap (algebraMap A B)))) :
    ∃ g ∈ q.primeCompl,
      algebraMap B (Localization.Away g) h ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.Away g) ∧
        ∀ q' : Ideal B, ∀ _ : q'.IsPrime, g ∉ q' →
          Module.Flat A (LocalizedModule.AtPrime q' (B ⧸ Ideal.span {h})) := by
  obtain ⟨hnzd, hflat⟩ := mem_nonZeroDivisors_atPrime_and_flat_quotient_of_fibre q hreg
  obtain ⟨g₁, hg₁, hreg₁⟩ := exists_notMem_mem_nonZeroDivisors_away q hhq hnzd
  obtain ⟨g₂, hg₂, hflat₂⟩ := exists_notMem_forall_flat_localizedModule_quotient q
    ((flat_localizedModule_quotient_iff q.primeCompl h).mp hflat)
  exact ⟨g₁ * g₂, q.primeCompl.mul_mem hg₁ hg₂,
    mem_nonZeroDivisors_away_mul_right hreg₁ g₂,
    fun q' hq' hg => hflat₂ q' hq' fun hc => hg (q'.mul_mem_left _ hc)⟩

end Spread

end Stacks.Flatness

end
